# Application config / secrets
#
# Deny-by-default so a developer's application-local.yml can never be committed.
# Every profile that is genuinely part of the build must be negated below, and
# every negation must be reviewed: adding one here is a decision to publish that
# file. Keep secrets in env vars regardless — see SECURITY.md.
#
# This rule is why application-docker.yml went missing: the profile was named in
# docker-compose.yml (SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=docker) but the file it referred to
# was silently untracked, so the containerized app fell back to localhost
# defaults and never reached the database.
**/src/main/resources/application-*.yml
**/src/main/resources/application-*.yaml
!**/src/main/resources/application.yml
!**/src/main/resources/application.yaml
!**/src/main/resources/application-endpoint.yml
!**/src/main/resources/application-endpoint.yaml
!**/src/main/resources/application-docker.yml
!**/src/main/resources/application-local.yml.example
branch_structure.json
temp_auto_push.bat
temp_interactive_push.bat

# NOTE: this file must never list itself. A .gitignore that ignores itself is
# silently absent from the repository, so every rule above protects only the
# machine it was written on — which is how the realm-export, .env and
# application-local.yml guards came to exist on one laptop and nowhere else.
